        <div class="event">
            <span class="date">April 15, 1989</span>
            <p>The death of former Communist Party General Secretary Hu Yaobang, a reformist leader, sparks student gatherings in Tiananmen Square to mourn his passing and call for political reforms.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="event">
            <span class="date">April 17–22, 1989</span>
            <p>Student protests grow, with thousands marching in Beijing. Demonstrations spread to other cities, including Shanghai and Wuhan. Protesters demand freedom of speech, a free press, and democratic reforms.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="event">
            <span class="date">April 26, 1989</span>
            <p>The <em>People's Daily</em> publishes an editorial condemning the protests as "turmoil," escalating tensions. Students respond with larger demonstrations, including a march of over 100,000 people in Beijing.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="event">
