            <p>Around 100,000 students and workers gather in Tiananmen Square for a mass rally. The movement gains widespread support from intellectuals, workers, and even some government officials.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="event">
            <span class="date">May 13, 1989</span>
            <p>Students begin a hunger strike in Tiananmen Square, drawing international attention. Over 1,000 protesters refuse food, and public sympathy grows.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="event">
            <span class="date">May 19, 1989</span>
            <p>Premier Li Peng declares martial law in Beijing, authorizing the military to suppress the protests. Troops begin moving toward the city.</p>
        </div>

